From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Omit the SNI Menu property without a D-Bus menu.

The SNI backend renders the application's own Win32 context menu. It does
not export com.canonical.dbusmenu, but advertises Menu=/NO_DBUSMENU. Plasma
recognizes this KDE-specific sentinel. Waybar 0.15 instead creates a
DbusmenuGtkMenu for any nonempty path and pops it up without calling
ContextMenu. Battle.net therefore gets a tiny empty GTK menu and no right
click notification.

Do not advertise Menu in GetAll or introspection, and return UnknownProperty
when it is requested explicitly. Hosts without a menu importer can then
use the existing ContextMenu method. Plasma already handles an absent Menu
property this way. Keep the separate Mutter/XEmbed fallback for GNOME's
AppIndicator host, whose click and menu handling also differ.

This is a follow-up to Erhan Bilgili (nanomatters)'s SNI backend imported
from https://github.com/nanomatters/wine-wineland; no native menu rendering
or graphics-driver changes are needed for the empty Waybar menu.

Related: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/803
References: https://github.com/Alexays/Waybar/blob/0.15.0/src/modules/sni/item.cpp
References: https://github.com/KDE/plasma-workspace/blob/master/applets/systemtray/statusnotifieritemsource.cpp
---

